[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: API low-level requirements
UID: FMD-LLR-API
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-22
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Low-level requirements of the API item, written from the code under `api/` as built. Parents are in
`hlr-api.sdoc`. The design is in `docs/lifecycle/06-design/lld-api.md`; the interfaces in
`03-system/icd/icd-http-api.md` and `03-system/icd/icd-storage.md`. Sizes: 1 MiB is 1048576 bytes. Times are
Unix seconds. "The token check" is LLR-API-013 applied through `check_airframe_token`.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Application, middleware and start-up (api/main.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Early size refusal
STATEMENT: >>>
For `POST /analyse` whose `Content-Length` header is all digits and greater than `MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB` x 1048576
+ 65536 bytes, `request_log` answers 413 `{"detail": "File too large. Maximum size is <n>MB."}` with
`X-Request-ID`, without calling the route and without reading the body.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Request id header
STATEMENT: >>>
`request_log` sets `X-Request-ID` on every response returned through it to the first 12 lower-case hexadecimal
characters of a new UUID4.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
An exception not handled inside the application is logged and re-raised; the 500 answer built outside the
middleware then carries no `X-Request-ID`, so "every response" of HLR-API-025 holds only for handled responses.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Request log line
STATEMENT: >>>
`_log_request` writes one INFO record to the logger `flightmd.access` per request: a JSON object with exactly
`request_id`, `method`, `route` (the matched route template, or `unmatched`), `status` and `ms` (duration
rounded to 0.1 ms). An exception from the application is logged with status 500.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test reads the access log. A review reads `_log_request` and checks that no raw path, client address or file
name is written.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Cross-origin settings
STATEMENT: >>>
The application wraps everything, the early 413 included, in `CORSMiddleware` with `allow_origins` set to the
comma-separated entries of `CORS_ORIGINS` (blank entries dropped), `allow_credentials` false, all methods and
headers allowed, and `X-Request-ID`, `X-FlightMD-Schema-Version` and `Content-Disposition` exposed.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test sends a cross-origin request. A review checks the `add_middleware(CORSMiddleware, ...)` call and that it
comes after the `request_log` middleware.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Trusted proxies checked at start-up
STATEMENT: >>>
`lifespan` first calls `trusted_networks(TRUSTED_PROXIES)`, which parses each comma-separated entry with
`ipaddress.ip_network(strict=False)`; an entry that is not an address or network raises `ValueError` and the
application does not start.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test starts the application with a bad `TRUSTED_PROXIES`. A review checks that the call is the first
statement of `lifespan` and is not inside a `try`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Start-up steps
STATEMENT: >>>
`_startup` sets `FLIGHTMD_DATA_DIR` in the process environment to the data directory when it is not set, runs
`import_legacy` on `api/data` and the data directory (LLR-API-108), and, with the in-process queue only, marks
every processing job interrupted (LLR-API-069) and deletes every file in `<data dir>/uploads`. It then runs one
sweep (LLR-API-007, LLR-API-008). With the Redis queue processing jobs and upload files are left alone.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-029

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Expiry sweep
STATEMENT: >>>
`_sweep` deletes the reports selected by `cleanup_expired(3600)` (LLR-API-068) and, for each deleted
identifier, its export directory (LLR-API-083).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stale jobs, old uploads and sweep period
STATEMENT: >>>
`_sweep` also runs `fail_stale(3600)` (LLR-API-070) and deletes the files in `<data dir>/uploads` last modified
more than 3600 s ago. `_cleanup_loop` runs `_sweep` in a worker thread every 600 s after start-up; an exception
from it is logged and the loop goes on.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests run `fail_stale` on the store and the start-up removal of uploads, not these steps of the sweep or the
loop. A review reads `_sweep`, `_remove_old_uploads` and `_cleanup_loop`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-011

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Settings (api/config.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Settings sources and defaults
STATEMENT: >>>
`Settings` reads environment variables (names not case sensitive) and the `.env` file in the repository root,
ignores names it does not know, and defaults to: `max_file_size_mb` 50, `rate_limit_per_hour` 10,
`ask_rate_limit_per_hour` 30, `pdf_rate_limit_per_hour` 30, `max_concurrent_analyses` 2, `cors_origins`
`http://localhost` and `http://127.0.0.1` on ports 3000, 3001 and 3100, `trusted_proxies` empty,
`allow_http_webhooks` false, `flightmd_data_dir` `data`, `flightmd_s3_bucket` empty, `flightmd_s3_prefix`
`contributions/`, `flightmd_s3_endpoint_url` and `flightmd_s3_region` empty, `flightmd_redis_url` empty,
`metrics_token` empty, `ai_provider` `groq`, `groq_api_key` and `anthropic_api_key` empty. `get_settings`
returns one cached instance per process.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test reads the defaults as a set; tests override single values. A review compares the `Settings` fields with
this list.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-032

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Derived settings
STATEMENT: >>>
`app_version` defaults to the installed `flightmd-core` version, or `0.0.0+local` when it is not installed;
`max_file_size_bytes` is `max_file_size_mb` x 1048576; `data_dir` is `flightmd_data_dir` made absolute against
the working directory; `ai_configured` is true only when `ai_provider`, trimmed and in lower case, is `groq` with
a non-empty `groq_api_key` or `anthropic` with a non-empty `anthropic_api_key`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test sets a provider and key and reads `ai_configured`, or runs without the package installed. A review reads
`_package_version` and the `Settings` properties.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
`app_version` is itself a setting, so an `APP_VERSION` variable replaces the package version on `/health` and in
export cache names.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-015
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-032

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Client address, rate limits and airframe tokens (api/security.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Client address
STATEMENT: >>>
`client_ip` returns the socket peer address (`unknown` when there is none) unless `TRUSTED_PROXIES` is set and
the peer is inside one of its networks. Then it splits every `X-Forwarded-For` header on commas and returns the
right-most entry that is not inside a trusted network, the left-most entry when all are trusted, or the peer when
there is no entry.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Rate limits
STATEMENT: >>>
One `slowapi` limiter keyed by `client_ip` limits `POST /analyse` to `RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR`,
`POST /ask/{report_id}` to `ASK_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR`, and `GET /export/pdf/{report_id}` and
`GET /export/airframe/{label}/pdf` each to `PDF_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR` requests per hour. A request over the limit
gets 429 from slowapi's handler. The limits are read when the modules are imported and counted in process
memory.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test drives a route past its limit (tests reset the limiter). A review checks each `@limiter.limit`
decorator, its limit string, and the exception handler added in `api/main.py`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
The counts live in each process's memory, so with several API processes each keeps its own count.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Token errors
STATEMENT: >>>
`token_error` maps the reason `invalid` to 403 "Wrong airframe token.", `missing` to 401 "This airframe needs
its X-Airframe-Token header." and `unclaimed` to 401 "Airframe not claimed yet. Saving its config, logging
maintenance or tagging an upload with it claims it.". `check_airframe_token` raises that error when
`authorise` (LLR-API-086) refuses the token.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Claim checked before the work
STATEMENT: >>>
`precheck_airframe_token` writes nothing; it returns true for an unclaimed airframe, false when the token fits,
and raises the 401 or 403 of LLR-API-013 for a missing or wrong token on a claimed one. A write route claims
only after its own checks pass, with `check_airframe_token(claim=True)`, which returns the new token.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-017

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Upload and dataset routes (api/routers/analyse.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Short file
STATEMENT: >>>
`POST /analyse` reads the first 4096 bytes of the field `file`; fewer than 8 bytes gives 400 "Invalid file. Must
be a PX4 ULog (.ulg), ArduPilot (.bin), or MAVLink telemetry (.tlog) file.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Format of an upload
STATEMENT: >>>
`_detect` returns format `compressed` with suffix `.gz` for content starting `1F 8B` and `.zip` for content
starting `50 4B 03 04`; otherwise the format from `detect_format_from_header(head, file name,
complete=len(head) < 4096)` with suffix `.ulg`, `.bin`, `.log`, `.tlog`, `.bbl`, `.txt` or `.dat` for
`px4_ulog`, `ardupilot_bin`, `ardupilot_log`, `mavlink_tlog`, `betaflight_bbl`, `dji_txt`, `dji_dat` (`.ulg`
for any other). `UnsupportedFormatError` gives 400 with the detector's message. A missing file name is taken as
`flight.ulg`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Label and brief hash checks
STATEMENT: >>>
After format detection and before the copy, a non-blank `airframe_label` that `normalise_airframe_label` turns
into none gives 400 "Invalid airframe label (no slashes or control characters).", and a non-blank
`planning_brief_sha256` that, trimmed, is not 64 hexadecimal characters gives 400 "planning_brief_sha256 must be
64 hex characters."; a valid hash is passed on in lower case. A blank label or hash counts as none.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Copy of the upload
STATEMENT: >>>
`_save_upload` copies the upload in reads of 1 MiB to a new file `flightmd-<random><suffix>` in
`<data dir>/uploads` (created when missing) and returns its path, size and SHA-256. When the running size passes
`MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB` x 1048576 bytes it stops and deletes the partial file, and the route answers 413 "File too
large. Maximum size is <n>MB."; any other error also deletes the partial file.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Duplicate upload
STATEMENT: >>>
When `contribute_to_dataset` is false and the request does not claim a new airframe, the route calls
`find_recent_duplicate(sha, label, brief, 3600)` (LLR-API-066). On a match it deletes the copied file, counts the
analysis with outcome `deduplicated` and answers 200 with `report_id` and `status` of the match,
`estimated_seconds` 0 when it is complete and 20 otherwise, and `deduplicated` true, creating no job.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Job store full
STATEMENT: >>>
The route creates the job row under a new UUID4 with `job_store.create`; when that raises `StoreFull`
(LLR-API-060) it deletes the copied file and answers 503 "Too many analyses in progress. Try again in a
minute.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The cap is tested on the store (LLR-API-060); no test fills the store and posts an upload. A review reads the
`except StoreFull` branch of `analyse_log`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Claim after the job row
STATEMENT: >>>
When the precheck found the label unclaimed, the route claims it after the job row is created. If the claim
fails (another request claimed it in between) the route deletes the job row with `discard`, deletes the copied
file and returns the 401 or 403. `discard` deletes the row and its parsed copy.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
The claim comes before the hand-over to the queue. When the hand-over then fails (LLR-API-022) the answer is
503 without the token, and the airframe stays claimed by a token nobody holds. This is a gap against
HLR-API-017 ("a request refused for another reason shall not consume the claim").
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Queue hand-over failure
STATEMENT: >>>
An exception from `get_queue().submit` marks the job failed with the error "could not be queued", deletes the
copied file and gives 503 "The analysis queue is unavailable. Try again in a minute.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Accepted upload answer
STATEMENT: >>>
After the hand-over the route answers 200 with `report_id`, `status` "processing", `estimated_seconds` 20 and
`deduplicated` false, plus `airframe_token` only when this request claimed the airframe and `contribution_id`
(the first 32 hexadecimal characters of the upload's SHA-256) only when `contribute_to_dataset` is true.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-027

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dataset statistics
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /dataset/stats` answers 200 `{"contributed_logs": <number of contributions>, "total_bytes": <sum of their
sizes>}` (LLR-API-107).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-027

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Withdraw a contribution
STATEMENT: >>>
`DELETE /dataset/{contribution_id}` answers 204 with no body when `training_data_store.delete` removed the
contribution (LLR-API-106), and 404 "No contribution with that id." when the id is not 32 lower-case
hexadecimal characters or nothing is stored under it. No token is asked.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
A withdrawal sent while the contributing analysis is still running answers 404, and the job then stores the
contribution (a to-do note in the code). Gap against HLR-API-027.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-027

