STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /status/{report_id}` answers 200 with the job summary (LLR-API-064), or 404 "Report not found or expired."
when the summary is `not_found`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-028
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Report route
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /report/{report_id}` answers 200 with the report serialised by `model_dump_json` as `application/json`
(a NaN float is written as null) and the header `X-FlightMD-Schema-Version` equal to the report's
`schema_version`; the other answers are those of LLR-API-026. No route lists reports or uploads.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-029
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Question route
STATEMENT: >>>
`POST /ask/{report_id}` takes the JSON body `{"question": <1 to 500 characters>}` (422 otherwise), applies
LLR-API-026, builds an `AIEnhancer` from `AI_PROVIDER`, `GROQ_API_KEY` and `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, and answers
`{"configured": false, "answer": null}` without an outbound call when it is not configured, else
`{"configured": true, "answer": <LLR-API-115>}`. It stores nothing.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
PR-023 confirmed: the route never reads `FLIGHTMD_OFFLINE` (`flightmd_core.orchestrator.offline()`), so with a
key set and offline mode on, the question and the cleaned report are still sent to the provider. Gap against
SYS-025.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-016

