[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Export routes (api/routers/export.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-030
STATUS: Active
TITLE: PDF export
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /export/pdf/{report_id}` returns the PDF from the export cache (kind `report.pdf`) as `application/pdf`
with `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="flightmd_report_<first 8 characters of the id>.pdf"`. A
`RuntimeError` from the renderer gives 501 "PDF export isn't available on this server."; any other exception
gives 500 "PDF generation failed.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-031
STATUS: Active
TITLE: GPX and KML export
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /export/gpx/{report_id}` and `GET /export/kml/{report_id}` give 422 "This flight log has no GPS track to
export." when `metadata.gps_path` is empty; otherwise they return the cached `track.gpx` as
`application/gpx+xml` named `flightmd_track_<8>.gpx`, or `track.kml` as `application/vnd.google-earth.kml+xml`
named `flightmd_track_<8>.kml`, as attachments. A build error gives 500 "GPX generation failed." or "KML
generation failed.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-032
STATUS: Active
TITLE: JSON export
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /export/json/{report_id}` returns the report as JSON indented by 2 spaces (cached as `report.json`), as the
attachment `flightmd_report_<8>.json` with `X-FlightMD-Schema-Version` equal to its `schema_version`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-033
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airframe record PDF
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /export/airframe/{label}/pdf` gives 400 "Invalid airframe label." for a label that normalises to none,
applies the token check, and renders (not cached) a PDF from the airframe's config, its maintenance status
(LLR-API-090) and one row per flight of LLR-API-067 with upload date (UTC, `YYYY-MM-DD`), file name, duration in
minutes to 1 decimal, score rounded to a whole number and grade. The answer is `application/pdf` with
`attachment; filename="flightmd_airframe_<ascii>.pdf"; filename*=UTF-8''<percent-encoded
flightmd_airframe_<label>.pdf>`, where `<ascii>` is the label with every character that is not an ASCII letter
or digit replaced by `_`. A render error gives 500 "PDF generation failed.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-020

