STATEMENT: >>>
`LocalQueue` runs `max(1, MAX_CONCURRENT_ANALYSES)` worker tasks that take jobs from an unbounded
`asyncio.Queue` in order and run them with `run_job`, so no more than that many run at once; an exception from
a job is logged and the worker goes on. Workers start on the first `submit` in an event loop; `depth` is the
number of jobs waiting.
