`authorise` reads the airframe in a transaction (a write transaction when claiming). With no stored token hash
it raises `TokenError("unclaimed")`, or with `claim=True` stores the SHA-256 hex of a new
`secrets.token_urlsafe(32)` token and returns the token. With a stored hash it raises `missing` for an empty
token and `invalid` when the token's SHA-256 differs (constant-time compare), and returns none when it fits.
