[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Metrics (api/metrics.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-100
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Analysis metrics
STATEMENT: >>>
`count_analysis` increments `flightmd_analyses_total{format, outcome}` and `observe_duration` records
`flightmd_analysis_duration_seconds{format}` (buckets 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 30, 60, 120, 300, 600 s); a format
outside the eight known values is `other`, an outcome outside `complete`, `rejected`, `error`, `deduplicated` is
`error`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
With the Redis queue these counters are kept in the worker processes, which serve no `/metrics`; the API's
`/metrics` then shows only HTTP metrics and `deduplicated`. Gap against HLR-API-026.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-026

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-API-101
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Metrics token
STATEMENT: >>>
When `METRICS_TOKEN` is set, `GET /metrics` gives 401 "Metrics need a bearer token." with
`WWW-Authenticate: Bearer` unless `Authorization` is `Bearer <token>` (scheme in any case), and 403 "Wrong
metrics token." when the token differs (constant-time compare); when it is empty the route is open. The answer
is the Prometheus text of the default registry.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-API-026

